; =============================================================================
; Secret of Evermore — Casual Run
; AUTHORITATIVE FLAT SOURCE — v1.28 ALWAYS-ON MINIMAP RELEASE
; =============================================================================
;
; PURPOSE OF THIS FILE
; --------------------
; This is the single authoritative ASM source for Secret of Evermore: Casual Run.
; Starting with v1.07, the project intentionally stops treating older versioned ASM
; files and separate architecture notes as required build context. The complete ROM
; mutation set, the source-recovery contract, expansion ownership, subsystem design,
; important WRAM/ROM facts, historical withdrawals, validation identity, and current
; future-development boundary are documented here beside the bytes they govern.
;
; v1.07 is the immutable SOURCE-ARCHITECTURE baseline: no intentional gameplay or ROM-byte
; change relative to accepted v1.06, therefore byte-identical to v1.06. v1.08 added the
; runtime-approved status-aware ordinary-drop system and Drain / Double Drain rebalance.
; v1.09 promotes the fully tested secondary-menu B-cancel/display cleanup, replaces Control
; Prefs with Dog Equipment on the Boy Ring, and makes the Dog main Ring inaccessible while
; preserving FuSoYa's P2 Start join/withdraw behavior. v1.10 ports black-sliver's Evermizer
; Tiny's-lair softlock fix: the gate-opening event no longer sets the persistent Tiny-gate flag
; before the encounter is resolved. v1.11 begins the final full-script review with the complete
; Fire Eyes / Elizabeth character pass while leaving the accepted gameplay baseline unchanged.
; v1.12-v1.14 continue the major-character script pass through Horace, Camellia, and
; Professor Ruffleberg/Carltron. v1.15 removes the largely redundant Targeting command
; from the Boy Main Ring; the native Ring builder then contracts the remaining choices.
; v1.16 reorganizes the live story script into documented regional raw-text arenas with
; reserved expansion room, without intentionally changing any dialogue or event behavior.
; v1.17 completes the full arena-by-arena story/world script review across all 25 documented
; regional arenas. It promotes the accepted wording, terminology, punctuation, presentation, and
; consistency fixes from that review without changing the frozen gameplay/control feature set.
; v1.18 replaces the earlier MSU dispatcher with the runtime-approved per-request fallback
; architecture: native SPC song data always initializes SFX, valid PCMs can mute only native
; music and play through MSU-1, and missing PCMs fall back without disabling later MSU tracks.
; v1.19 promotes the runtime-approved dialogue-presentation baseline: Window Edit is removed
; from the accessible Boy Main Ring, and every ordinary dialogue helper $02-$0B uses the
; native five-line height while retaining its original horizontal family/position. v1.20 then
; consolidates all reachable ordinary-dialogue callers to canonical helper $03 (Family A) or
; $08 (Family B). The eight retired geometry IDs retain alias pointers as a stable safety net,
; and Jade's early-Yes response gains the missing authored $86 player-advance wait.
; v1.21 promotes the accepted event-owned ordinary-dialogue presentation used by Omnitopia
; arrival/transit scenes. v1.22 performs the broader Phase-2 lifecycle cleanup: event-owned
; open/close behavior, canonical narration/speaker normalization, redundant-page cleanup,
; border-first teardown, and the surgical Podunk-opening lifecycle repair.
; v1.23 is the first accepted theme-foundation release. The reclaimed $02-$18 helper pool now
; carries dedicated presentation identities: $02 Narration/System, $03 Generic NPC, $04 Boy,
; $05 Robot, $06 Comedic Relief, $07 Alchemist, and $08-$18 reserved theme slots. Helper
; identity drives pattern/border application without inferring theme from geometry. Boy uses
; x=$01 y=$12 w=$1E h=$06 and the Podunk $1944 pattern; Generic/Evermore uses $19A4;
; Robot/synthetic uses $1934. Carltron's verified Omnitopia introduction beats use Robot $05.
; v1.24 freezes the semantic helper roster through $17, corrects theme routing to decode
; $51/$52 as byte offsets into the 3-byte TEXT pointer table, and separates speaker/category
; assignment from helper-owned visual styling. v1.25 promotes the tested initial theming
; standards: every semantic helper has table-driven geometry/pattern/border behavior, audited
; fixed-owner category routes are applied, Fire Eyes Village speaker corrections are folded in,
; and the Save Game A/B presentation/input follow-up is accepted. A full-game QA run remains
; required to catch any missed or misapplied theme callsites; that review is now coverage QA
; against the v1.25 standards rather than another redesign of the theme architecture. v1.26
; begins isolated post-v1.25 feature work while that external QA proceeds: Barrier duration is
; reduced from 2700 to 1800 frames (~45s -> ~30s), Atlas from 5400 to 3600 frames (~90s ->
; ~60s), and Crush base might from 62 to 61. No other intentional gameplay/presentation change.
; v1.27 promotes the runtime-approved DSP-1 Windwalker world-map camera: the cartridge is
; declared DSP-1, Evermore's native Mode-7 HDMA buffers are filled from DSP-1 Op $02/$0A
; perspective matrices, heading uses the calibrated (-heading + 90 degrees) basis, and native
; Windwalker yaw integration is reduced to 50% while preserving the original acceleration curve.
; The existing full-map toggle and landing behavior remain otherwise unchanged in this release.
; v1.28 promotes the runtime-approved native Windwalker minimap repair. The clean original
; world-map OBJ graphics block is relocated to expansion ROM because an older recovered code
; allocation overlaps the original $C5:6FBB-$C5:77BA graphics source. The native minimap dots,
; landing markers, position math, and OAM layout are retained, and the lower-left minimap is
; forced visible during flight. No altitude-rate/control experiment is included.
;
