; 6. TEXT ENGINE / v1.04 DIALOGUE-ROUTING ARCHITECTURE
; =============================================================================
;
; PRIMARY POINTER TABLE
;   PC $11D000, 3,002 entries, 3 bytes each.
;
; ORIGINAL PACKED-POINTER DECODE
;   pc = (raw24 & $007FFF) | ((raw24 & $7F8000) << 1)
;   Bit 23 distinguishes compressed dialogue from raw/ascii-style payloads in the
;   original decoder.
;
; CLEAN-ROM COMPRESSION DATA
;   DTE pairs                 PC $11F32E
;   scatter table             PC $11F3AE
;   8-bit dictionary ptrs     PC $11F3EC
;   16-bit dictionary ptrs    PC $11F46C
;   8-bit dictionary strings  PC $11F66C
;   16-bit dictionary strings PC $11F7D5
;
; REFERENCE DUMPS
;   reference/text/SoE_USA_script_dump_with_locations.txt
;   reference/text/SoE_USA_script_index.csv
;   These contain pointer locations, raw pointer bytes, payload locations, compression
;   mode, original footprint, and decoded text for every primary entry.
;
; v1.04 RAW-TEXT ROUTING
;   Native hooks at $CC:CD0C-$CC:CD16 and $CC:CD4A-$CC:CD54 replace only the raw /
;   uncompressed text-bank resolution tails. Compressed-text branches preserve their
;   original destinations.
;
;   If a raw text pointer resolves to bank $F2, the selector tests $7E22E9 bit $10:
;     clear -> normal text remains in $F2
;     set   -> substitute mirrored NG+ text bank $F3
;   Other banks pass through unchanged.
;
;
