; 9. v1.06-v1.09 FINAL CONTROLS ARCHITECTURE
; =============================================================================
;
; FINAL PLAYER-FACING CONTROL MAP
;   A       action / interaction / attack / confirm (former B role)
;   B       walk + Casual Run accelerated charge in field (former A role)
;   B       Cancel/Back while Ring is open
;   B       Back/Exit on secondary management screens
;   Start   open Boy Main Ring; Cancel/Back while Ring is open
;   Select  switch controlled character in the field; no-op while Ring is open
;   X       open Boy Item Ring directly
;   Y       open Boy Alchemy Ring directly
;
; MULTIPLAYER CONTRACT
;   The A/B role swap applies to both controllers.
;   P1 alone receives Start/X/Y Ring shortcuts. Start always opens the Boy Ring, even
;   when P1 currently controls Dog. P2 receives no pause/menu shortcut; P2 Start retains
;   FuSoYa's existing multiplayer enable/disable behavior. Do not rewrite the P2 Start block.
;
; WHY DIRECT RING SHORTCUTS
;   Experimental smart-heal and repeat-last-alchemy implementations were discarded.
;   Direct Item/Alchemy access is consistently useful, faster than vanilla, flexible,
;   predictable, and keeps all actual item/formula selection inside native game systems.
;
; REMEMBERED-PAGE IMPLEMENTATION
;   SoE already remembers Ring page per character. Ring manager indexes state from
;   $7E:0090 + Menu Ring Character.
;
;   Boy menu-character pointer $4E89 -> remembered page $7E:4F19
;   Dog menu-character pointer $4F37 -> remembered page $7E:4FC7
;
;   Boy page-list offsets used by shortcuts:
;     $0000 Main
;     $0002 Alchemy
;     $0004 Weapon
;     $0008 Item
;     $0006 is conditional/other and is not used by these shortcuts.
;
;   Shortcut behavior:
;     Start -> write $0000 to $7E:4F19, establish ordinary Boy Ring
;     X     -> write $0008 to $7E:4F19, establish ordinary Boy Ring
;     Y     -> write $0002 to $7E:4F19, establish ordinary Boy Ring
;
;   There is NO synthetic Up/Down injection and NO post-open page-transition hook.
;   Native page transition routine $CE:ADBC-$CE:ADC3 and FuSoYa direction dispatcher
;   $F0:0300-$F0:0302 remain untouched from v1.05.
;
; CONTROLLER / ACTOR ROUTING
;   FuSoYa dynamically routes physical controllers into Boy/Dog actor input words. The
;   field shortcut helpers are therefore attached to both actor paths and test ownership
;   before honoring P1 Start/X/Y. A temporary flag forces a P1 shortcut-opened Boy Ring
;   to continue reading P1 input if physical P1 currently owns Dog.
;
; TRANSIENT FLAG
;   $7E:32F0 = nonzero while a P1 shortcut-opened Boy Ring must read P1 even if P1 owns
;   Dog. It is not saved game state and is cleared on field return.
;
; CONTROL ALLOCATIONS / HOOKS
;   $F0:0013-$F0:0015  P1 raw A/B-swap hook
;   $F0:002F-$F0:0031  P2 raw A/B-swap hook
;   $F0:00AD-$F0:00AF  bypass only P1 Start multiplayer branch
;   $F0:0250-$F0:0259  A/B swap trampolines
;   $F0:0328-$F0:0333  forced-P1 Ring-input return helper
;   $F0:0338-$F0:033E  controller-aware Select test
;   $F0:0343-$F0:0345  Ring Cancel mask = physical B + Start
;   $F0:0962-$F0:0964  redirect P2 Ring-input return through forced-P1 helper
;   $CE:AE71-$CE:AE76  Ring-owner switch uses controller-aware Select
;   $CF:CDDD+          Boy actor field shortcut hook
;   $CF:CF10+          Dog actor field shortcut hook
;   $F7:0014           Jaguar Ring tutorial letter -> B
;   $F5:0000-$F5:005C Boy actor shortcut dispatcher
;   $F5:0100-$F5:015C Dog actor shortcut dispatcher
;   $F5:0200-$F5:0232 Boy Ring establishment + menu-entry Boy-window baseline
;   $F5:0800-$F5:0814 P1 A/B swap helper
;   $F5:0820-$F5:0834 P2 A/B swap helper
;   v1.08 secondary-menu input overrides:
;     $F0:0370, $F0:0380, $F0:03D0, $F0:03E0, $F0:03F0, $F0:0430, $F0:0450
;     $CD:92F1/$CD:93E6, $CD:95E9/$CD:96DE, $CD:98D4/$CD:99C9
