; =============================================================================
; v1.06 — final control overhaul
; =============================================================================
; The final v1.06 design intentionally uses direct Ring shortcuts rather than
; smart-item or repeat-alchemy automation. The field shortcuts choose which native Boy ring page
; should be remembered, then invoke the ordinary Boy ring establishment path:
;
;   A       = former B role (action / attack / confirm)
;   B       = former A role in the field (walk / accelerated charge)
;             and Cancel/Back while a ring is open
;   Start   = open Boy Main ring; Cancel/Back while a ring is open
;   Select  = switch Boy/Dog ring owner while a ring is open
;   X       = open Boy Item ring directly
;   Y       = open Boy Alchemy ring directly
;
; X/Y/Start shortcuts are physical-controller-1 features. Player 2 receives none
; of these menu shortcuts. P2 Start remains FuSoYa's existing multiplayer toggle.
;
; Native ring-page memory:
;   The ring manager reads/writes an indexed state at $7E:0090 + Menu Ring Character.
;   For the Boy pointer $4E89 this resolves to $7E:4F19; for Dog $4F37 it is
;   $7E:4FC7. These shortcuts always open the Boy ring, so they preload $7E:4F19. For the Boy page list
;   ($8E:998C), the useful remembered offsets are:
;       $0000 = Main
;       $0002 = Alchemy
;       $0004 = Weapon
;       $0008 = Item
;   (offset $0006 is a conditional page and is not used by these shortcuts.)
;
; Therefore this build does NOT synthesize Up/Down input and does NOT hook the
; native page-transition routine at $CE:ADBC. Start/X/Y simply preload $7E:4F19
; and establish the Boy ring.
;
; Transient WRAM:
;   $7E:32F0 = nonzero while a P1 shortcut-opened Boy ring should force P1 input
;              even when physical P1 currently owns Dog. Cleared on field return.
;

; --- P1 Start no longer participates in multiplayer join/withdraw --------------
; The corresponding P2 Start block at $F0:00E6 remains untouched.
org $F000AD
V106_SkipP1StartMultiplayerToggle:
    db $80, $37, $EA              ; BRA $F0:00E6 / NOP

