; =============================================================================
; v1.08 TEST — secondary management menus: physical B = Back/Exit (input only)
; =============================================================================
; v1.06 globally swaps the physical A/B roles before FuSoYa's controller-aware menu
; helpers see the input. Therefore physical B arrives in these legacy handlers as logical
; A bit $0080, while the old secondary-menu cancel convention is still logical Y $4000.
;
; The first menu-input test translated $0080->$4000 inside each F0 helper, but its final
; BIT/branch left the processor Z flag describing only "was B pressed?" instead of whether
; the helper's filtered input word was zero. Several callers intentionally use that Z flag
; immediately after JSL for key-repeat/debounce. Result: Action and Window Prefs ran at
; uncontrolled repeat speed, and R was rejected on Trade Goods and Alchemy Formulas.
;
; Corrected design: keep each inherited F0 helper's original contract — return the filtered
; input word with N/Z set from that complete word — while still translating accepted
; physical B into the legacy Y cancel bit. Each helper therefore performs its normal
; controller-aware fetch + mask, calls one common translator at $F5:1200, and returns.
; The translator changes $0080->$4000 only when B is present, then ORA #$0000 restores N/Z
; exactly from the final 16-bit input word. Carry and registers other than A are untouched.
;
; Action Screen is one special downstream case: after its repeat helper it re-fetches raw
; controller input before the final legacy Y/Start exit test. Patch that local exit test to
; physical B/Start directly. This is why changing only $F0:0380 could never make B exit the
; Action Screen reliably.
;
; Alchemy Setup, Charms/Rare Items, and the three Weapon Level family pages do their own
; local input masking, so their direct patches from the first test remain appropriate.
; This pass still changes no button legends, tiles, graphics, or explanatory text.

; Shared helper template (11 bytes; remaining recovered padding is left untouched):
;   JSR $0939 / AND #screen-mask / JSL $F5:1200 / RTL

org $F00370
