; =============================================================================
; v1.08 TEST 2 — replace Control Prefs with Dog Equipment on the main Ring
; =============================================================================
; The former Control Prefs Ring object is repurposed as Dog Equipment while the
; ordinary Boy Equipment object is left untouched.
;
; DISPLAY
; -------
; The old controller-preferences icon uses sprite block $07DF.  Instead of pointing
; the Ring object at the standalone Leather Collar item icon, reuse that exact old
; controller block slot/data area for a purpose-built 16x16 Dog Equip icon:
;   - top five rows copy the native green "EQUIP" legend from block $07DE
;   - lower rows contain a compact collar drawn with the Ring palette
; The replacement compresses to exactly the controller block's original 80 bytes,
; so no graphics relocation or pointer-table change is required.  $C4:559A is
; restored to its native $C8:00E6 animation script, which still resolves to block
; $07DF; only the pixels stored in that old controller block have changed.
;
; ACTION / RETURN
; ---------------
; Selecting the slot enters the native Equipment action with the Dog as the current
; Ring actor, but the saved parent page is the Boy main Ring ($998C, rather than the
; Dog main Ring $9998).  A transient $7E:32F2 flag marks this special entry.
;
; The central Ring cancel check at $CE:AE2C is wrapped.  On B/Start cancel while
; the special Dog Equipment flag is active, the wrapper restores Menu Ring Character
; to the Boy before native cancel processing runs, clears the flag, and returns the
; original cancel mask unchanged.  Thus backing out returns directly to the Boy Ring.
; Normal Dog Equipment reached through the Dog Ring is unaffected.
;
; $7E:32F2 = transient "Dog Equipment opened from Boy Ring" flag (v1.08 test 2)

