; =============================================================================
; v1.08 TEST 3B — Boy Ring only, P1 access only
; =============================================================================
; Supersedes the withdrawn TEST 3 approach that attempted to dedicate P2 Start to
; Ring access.  FuSoYa's P2 Start join/withdraw handler remains exactly as it was
; in TEST 2 / v1.06.  The established actor-local field shortcut dispatchers already
; provide the desired ownership rule:
;   * P1 Start opens the Boy Main Ring whether P1 currently controls Boy or Dog.
;   * P1 X/Y retain the Boy Item / Boy Alchemy direct shortcuts.
;   * P2 receives no Ring shortcut; P2 Start remains FuSoYa multiplayer join/withdraw.
;
; Only the Ring-local Select owner-swap is removed.  Do NOT alter the shared Select
; helper at $F0:0338: field Select still needs the normal FuSoYa character-control
; switching path.  Instead force only the native Ring owner-switch test at $CE:AE71
; to see zero.  The following native BEQ then takes the exact existing no-switch path.
;
; Native bytes here in TEST 2:
;   JSL $F0:0338 / NOP / NOP / BEQ +$09
; Replacement:
;   LDA #$0000 / NOP / NOP / NOP / BEQ +$09
; Thus Select is a harmless no-op while a Ring is open, while field Select remains
; untouched and can continue switching Boy/Dog control normally.
org $CEAE71
V108_BoyRingOnly_P1Only_DisableRingSelect:
    db $A9, $00, $00, $EA, $EA, $EA


