; =============================================================================
; post-v1.18 — THEME SAFETY HOTFIX / ROLLBACK
; =============================================================================
; Theme Passes 01-04 are intentionally NOT active in this safety build.
;
; Root cause found during Pass 04 QA:
;   * The prior theme prototypes rewrote global-script pointer entries $A4-$BF
;     after checking only literal A3 <ID> call sites.
;   * That ownership test was insufficient.  SoE can also call the same global
;     script table through opcode $B0 (global call with arguments), so non-A3
;     callers can still depend on those entries.
;   * The original v1.18 table contains live native pointers in that range.
;     Overwriting them can redirect unrelated event logic and caused the observed
;     late-game cutscene jump during the mansion/transport sequence.
;   * Pass 04 also mechanically converted cinematic $50 slot text to $51 windowed
;     text.  Those text payloads contain positioning/presentation controls authored
;     for the unwindowed path, producing the clipped/misaligned lab text seen in QA.
;
; Safety rule going forward:
;   - Do not reclaim a global-script ID based only on A3-call absence.
;   - Before reusing any global ID, account for every call form that can address the
;     global-script table, especially A3 and B0.
;   - Do not mechanically convert $50/$52 cinematic text to $51; audit the payload
;     controls and event presentation first.
;   - Perform the planned text/speaker ownership pass before the next theme rollout.
;
; This build intentionally returns to the accepted v1.18 + No Window Edit behavior
; as the clean QA baseline.  Theme design/table documentation is retained separately;
; no experimental theme-helper pointer hijacks are present here.
; =============================================================================


; =============================================================================
; v1.19 — STANDARDIZE ALL ORDINARY DIALOGUE HELPERS TO 5 LINES
; =============================================================================
; Runtime QA established that legitimate ordinary presentations (including choice
; boxes) can require the full native five-line capacity. The ordinary dialogue
; system therefore uses one fixed vertical geometry rather than varying height to
; match the amount of text in a particular beat.
;
; Horizontal families remain unchanged:
;   Family A: X=$0A, Y=$02, W=$14
;   Family B: X=$02, Y=$02, W=$14
;
; Every ordinary helper $02-$0B now uses height $08. Helpers $03 and $08 were
; already native five-line helpers and need no override. Helper IDs/callers are
; deliberately left intact in v1.19; post-release work may migrate ordinary calls
; to canonical $03 (Family A) / $08 (Family B) only after complete A3/B0 auditing.
;
; Family A legacy helpers -> five-line height.
org $D29E1D
V119_Helper02_Height5:
    db $08
org $D29E2B
V119_Helper04_Height5:
    db $08
org $D29E32
V119_Helper05_Height5:
    db $08
org $D29E39
V119_Helper06_Height5:
    db $08

; Family B legacy helpers -> five-line height.
org $D29E40
V119_Helper07_Height5:
    db $08
org $D29E4E
V119_Helper09_Height5:
    db $08
org $D29E55
V119_Helper0A_Height5:
    db $08
org $D29E5C
V119_Helper0B_Height5:
    db $08


; =============================================================================
; v1.20 — CONSOLIDATE ORDINARY DIALOGUE HELPER IMPLEMENTATIONS
; =============================================================================
; v1.19 standardized helpers $02-$0B to two byte-identical five-line geometry
; families.  This QA pass consolidates the GLOBAL SCRIPT POINTER TABLE itself:
;
;   Family A legacy IDs $02,$04,$05,$06 -> canonical helper $03 ($001E1F)
;   Family B legacy IDs $07,$09,$0A,$0B -> canonical helper $08 ($001E42)
;
; This is deliberately call-form agnostic: both A3 direct calls and B0 calls with
; arguments resolve through this same pointer table.  Event-script callsites are
; NOT rewritten in this pass, so the legacy IDs remain reserved aliases and are
; NOT yet available for reuse.
;
; Global pointer table base: $D2:990B, 3 bytes per ID.

; Family A aliases -> helper $03.
org $D29911                          ; ID $02
