; =============================================================================
; AUTHORITATIVE TEXT SOURCE / THEME ASSIGNMENT REGISTRY
; =============================================================================
; This is the forward-looking source of truth for every primary TEXT ID.  The project
; no longer records original/current/planned style snapshots here.  Each row answers:
;   source      = who/what owns the spoken or system text;
;   assignment  = how ownership is resolved (fixed, arena-default, caller-inherit,
;                 caller-fragment, page-map, or scene-actor);
;   theme       = the semantic theme/category selected for that source;
;   helper      = the dedicated theme helper used by an ordinary framed event beat.
;
; PAGE_MAP means one payload contains multiple speakers and must switch only at an audited
; page/window boundary. SCENE_ACTOR means the payload's visible cutscene actor still needs
; event-level resolution. INHERIT means a control/fragment never establishes a theme itself.
;
; Style is deliberately NOT tracked per TEXT.  Geometry, pattern, border, and later visual
; refinements belong to the helper/theme definition once, not to thousands of text rows.
; Storage arena is likewise not a theme: assignment follows the actual speaker/source.
;
; Maintenance rule: when ownership/category changes, update this row and the audited event
; helper call(s) that open its ordinary framed beat.  Do not infer from nearest storage arena.
; =============================================================================
; === BEGIN AUTHORITATIVE TEXTMETA REGISTRY ===
