; =============================================================================
; PHASE 2 QA — OWNER-CLOSE MESSAGE LIFECYCLE
; =============================================================================
; Supersedes the preceding experimental "clear on next presentation" lifecycle.
;
; FINAL LIFECYCLE INVARIANT FOR THIS QA:
;   * A presentation helper OPENS geometry only.
;   * It never erases a previous presentation.
;   * A player-dismissed dialogue is closed by the event/dialogue that opened it.
;   * A timed/cinematic message is closed by that cutscene's authored timing/clear.
;   * The following presentation is never responsible for wiping its predecessor.
;
; This fixes the visible upper-left -> lower-right flash in the first Omnitopia
; conversation.  TEXT 2915/2916 were incorrectly documented/classified as Carltron;
; both are Boy dialogue. Their event already opens helper $08, so the correct class
; is B / Upper Left and the text dispatcher must not replace that opener with A.
;
; The pre-arrival 2901-2912 Boy sequence is also converted at the EVENT level:
; native slot-1 $47 openers become $08, $50 slot-1 text/control calls become $51,
; and the cutscene's already-authored clears remain responsible for dismissal.
;
; Solo escape-pod Boy dialogue 2924 and 2927-2932 likewise opens $08 directly.
; =============================================================================

