; =============================================================================
; PHASE 2 QA — BORDER-FIRST WINDOW TEARDOWN
; =============================================================================
; Runtime QA indicates the remaining ordinary close looks layered in the wrong
; visual order: text disappears, then the patterned interior, while the frame
; survives long enough to read as a separate final wipe.
;
; Native full-container teardown $8C:ADF6 has a close-only call at $8C:AEB9 to
; $8C:B05F, the framed-window border-row renderer also used by the normal window
; update path. During teardown that call keeps rebuilding the frame as the backing
; rows are erased. For this QA, suppress ONLY the close-time border redraw. The
; normal $8C:AD9E -> $8C:B05F update/open path remains untouched, so framed boxes
; still draw normally; the close is allowed to erase the existing frame before
; the patterned interior finishes disappearing.
;
