; v1.25 RELEASE — COMPLETE SEMANTIC THEME STYLE PASS
; =============================================================================
; This block is the authoritative visual definition for the semantic helper roster
; established by v1.24. Text/event assignments are unchanged except for the audited
; fixed-owner corrections documented later in this release. A theme helper now owns its normal
; framed geometry plus one pattern/border pair; TEXT rows continue to record source/category/helper only.
;
; User-fixed / previously-tested contracts preserved here:
;   * $02 Narration/System is unchanged.
;   * $03 Generic NPC keeps x=$04 y=$02 w=$18 h=$08 and $19A4; only its requested
;     border changes from transparent $0014 to Boy-minimal $000E so the advance arrow
;     remains visible.
;   * $04 Boy remains x=$01 y=$12 w=$1E h=$06, $1944/$000E.
;   * $05 Robot keeps the tested right-side terminal x=$13 y=$01 w=$0C; its height is
;     now $14 after the latest runtime QA reduction, with thicker Boy-like border $0012.
;     Robot/synthetic pattern remains $1934.
;   * $16 Cecil deliberately reuses Boy-minimal border $000E; its unique $1974 pattern
;     and upper/mid placement distinguish it from Boy.
;
; For the remaining semantic categories, geometry is varied modestly while retaining
; five-line height $08 to avoid invalidating authored page boundaries.  Widths are kept
; at or above the old ordinary-dialogue width; Robot is the deliberate narrow exception
; already covered by the engine's native geometry-aware wrapping.  Artificial doubles
; mirror their real counterpart's border/geometry while swapping to synthetic $1934.
